      "thinking": "The shop waits synchronously on the pricing call with no timeout, and that call belongs to another team's service\u2014so the real issue sits in io-pricing. Since the page is still useful without the basket total, I'm thinking the fix is giving io-shop its own time budget: if pricing takes too long, treat it as unavailable rather than blocking, though the callable being synchronous complicates how that budget gets enforced after the call returns its duration.\n\nCapping the wait would mean running it with a timeout, but the docstring already states the shop doesn't retry or price itself when the service is slow \u2014 which makes me wonder if this is actually a \"nothing to change\" case, since io-shop is healthy and just correctly reporting slowness. Still, a real deadline would let pages render quickly without the basket total instead of waiting over a second, which seems like a genuine win worth pursuing, though adding a timeout to a synchronous callable or changing its interface risks breaking callers outside this repo. I want to check how the payment_provider handles this to see if there's already a consistent timeout pattern I should follow.\n\n",
